{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778979612194,"sessionID":"ses_1cc8fcfc1ffeVdeevBdyN2FfAy","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_Az6Eh3VpqeMY2TPd9N81YqpZ","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n+Implemented the requested new terms for stem cell memory T cells and committed the ontology changes locally.\n+\n+Added:\n+- `stem cell memory CD4-positive, alpha-beta T cell`\n+- `stem cell memory CD8-positive, alpha-beta T cell`\n+\n+These changes are committed in PR #<NN>.\n+\n+I kept this ticket focused on the two requested new terms. The species-specific modeling questions raised in the thread were not folded into this edit.\n*** Add File: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/PR_COMMENTS.md\n+Added two new Cell Ontology terms requested in issue `#3452`:\n+\n+- `CL_9900001` `stem cell memory CD4-positive, alpha-beta T cell`\n+- `CL_9900002` `stem cell memory CD8-positive, alpha-beta T cell`\n+\n+What changed:\n+- Added declarations for both new classes in `src/ontology/cl-edit.owl`.\n+- Added labels, text definitions, issue tracking annotation, contributor ORCIDs, creator, and timestamps.\n+- Added requested exact synonyms for both CD4 and CD8 TSCM terms.\n+- Placed the new terms under the existing memory T-cell parents:\n+  - CD4 TSCM under `CL_0000897` `CD4-positive, alpha-beta memory T cell`\n+  - CD8 TSCM under `CL_0000909` `CD8-positive, alpha-beta memory T cell`\n+\n+Rationale:\n+- The issue requested two new stem cell memory T-cell subset terms rather than species-specific subclasses.\n+- The comment thread raised broader species-specific modeling questions for memory T-cell subsets, but also noted that this should be handled in a separate ticket, so I kept this change scoped to the concrete NTR.\n+- The definitions follow the request text and are supported by the cited literature on T memory stem cells and their long-lived, self-renewing, multipotent properties.\n+\n+References used in the definitions and/or synonym support:\n+- `PMID:19525962`\n+- `PMID:21926977`\n+- `PMID:28060797`\n+\n+Validation performed:\n+- Confirmed the requested terms were not already present in `src/ontology/cl-edit.owl`.\n+- Checked the existing hierarchy for the CD4 and CD8 memory T-cell parent classes.\n+- Ran a ROBOT syntax conversion check:\n+  - `robot convert -i src/ontology/cl-edit.owl -o /tmp/opencode/cl-edit-validated.owl`\n+\n+Checklist completed:\n+- [x] Read imported issue context\n+- [x] Verified existing parent terms in the ontology\n+- [x] Added two new `CL_99xxxxx` terms\n+- [x] Added definitions with literature references\n+- [x] Added requested ORCID contributors\n+- [x] Added issue tracker annotation\n+- [x] Performed syntax validation with ROBOT\n+- [x] Committed only the ontology edit\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\nA PR_COMMENTS.md","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n===================================================================\n--- /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n+++ /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@\n+Implemented the requested new terms for stem cell memory T cells and committed the ontology changes locally.\n+\n+Added:\n+- `stem cell memory CD4-positive, alpha-beta T cell`\n+- `stem cell memory CD8-positive, alpha-beta T cell`\n+\n+These changes are committed in PR #<NN>.\n+\n+I kept this ticket focused on the two requested new terms. The species-specific modeling questions raised in the thread were not folded into this edit.\n\nIndex: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/PR_COMMENTS.md\n===================================================================\n--- /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/PR_COMMENTS.md\n+++ /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/PR_COMMENTS.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,38 @@\n+Added two new Cell O